==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɡuːp/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-goop.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːp}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{lb|en|informal|usually|uncountable}} A [[thick]], [[slimy]] [[substance]]; [[goo]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Olivia Judson|authorlink=Olivia Judson|title=The hemiparasite season [print version: Under the hemiparasite, ''International New York Times'', 24–25 December 2014, page&nbsp;7]|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/24/opinion/the-hemiparasite-season.html|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20141223181330/https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/24/opinion/the-hemiparasite-season.html|archivedate=23 December 2014|newspaper={{w|The New York Times}}|date=23 December 2014|passage=The flesh [of the [[mistletoe]] berry] is sticky, and forms strings and ribbons between my thumb and forefinger. For the mistletoe, this viscous '''goop'''&nbsp;– and by the way, viscous comes to English from {{l|la|viscum}}&nbsp;– is crucial. The stickiness means that, after eating the berries, birds often regurgitate the seeds and then wipe their bills on twigs&nbsp;– leading to the seeds' getting glued to the tree, where they can germinate and begin the cycle anew.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|informal|derogatory|dated}} A [[silly]], [[stupid]], or [[boorish]] person.
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1963
|author=P.G. Wodehouse
|title=Stiff Upper Lip, Jeeves
|section=chapter 22
|passage=I pointed out that Stiffy, who is pure padded cell from the foundation up, was planning to marry the Rev. H.P. Pinker, himself as pronounced a '''goop''' as ever preached the Hivites and Hittites}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|goopy}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} To [[apply]] a [[thick]], [[slimy]], or [[goo]]-like substance.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author={{w|William Gibson}}|title=The Peripheral
|url=
|text=Airstream, 1977. He showed her ones on eBay that looked like blunt rifle slugs, went for crazy money in any condition at all. The uncle had '''gooped''' this one over with white expansion foam, gone gray and dirty now, to stop it leaking and for insulation.
}}
# {{lb|en|informal|possibly|obsolete}} To [[stare]]; [[gawk]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1925|title=Alabaster Lamps|author=Margaret Turnbull
|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=wvwLAQAAMAAJ&q=%22gooping%22
|text=Young John blushed at being found “'''gooping'''” at himself in the glass.
}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1955|title=Ring Up the Curtain: Four Plays
|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=zHVKAAAAIAAJ&q=%22gooped+at%22
|text=He always said vegetables are grown to be eaten, not '''gooped''' at. Even a donkey doesn't want a carrot a foot long. I've always remembered. Of course he never won a thing at the Show.
}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1968|author={{w|Chrstianna Brand}}|section=The Hornet's Nest|title=What Dread Hand: A Collection of Short Stories
|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=a7EwL-a8-WEC&pg=PT65&lpg=PT65&dq=%22men+gooped+at%22
|text=it was dreadful, it was frightening, to be the sort of woman that, for some unknown reason, all men looked at, all men '''gooped''' at, all men—wanted.
}}

